            <ArticleTitle>[Allergic rhinitis in children as a risk factor of bronchial asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study was designed to measure hyperreactivity of bronchi in patients aged from 7-8 to 13-14 years presenting with allergic rhinitis. The efficiency of the bronchoprovocative test with physical exercises was shown to be higher than the study of external respiratory function at rest.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
